the champions league final with the stad  de france was delayed by 36 minutes  because of problems outside the stadium  sky news forensic team has analyzed  available video to see how events  unfolded in paris  problems began shortly after 6 45 pm  local time more than two hours before  the game was due to start  a large proportion of the 20 000  liverpool fans with tickets were headed  for this underpass on the south west  side of the stadium  in this video we can see fans were  forced to walk through a narrow gap in  between these police vehicles  film from the other side of the  underpass this next video shows just how  many police fans had lined the street  making the flow of fans harder some  taking four hours to get to this ramp  just 100 meters away  sky news has spoken to fans in this  video who say non-ticket holders were  also joining the queues  the checkpoint at the start of the ramp  was the main one used by liverpool  ticket holders  at this point we've counted five  stewards checking tickets security were  wearing yellow vests and doing searches  space was tight and they were struggling  to process the large number of people  trying to get in  slightly later at the same place some  people were filmed jumping over the side  of the ramp to get to the concourse  past that checkpoint people were inside  the concourse but not through the ticket  barriers  the french interior minister says that  more than 2  600 fake tickets made it inside  at gateway there were large crowds  around the turnstile entrance  in this video from the same gate but  inside the stadium stewards and police  can be seen holding people back  paramedics are attending a man on the  floor  the ticket gates were closed by security  several times because of people trying  to force their way through  they opened this additional gate to help  but shortly after police used pepper  spray to disperse this crowd  in this video filmed at gate x you can  see adults and children moving away  this man is helping a young child remove  pepper spray from his eyes  on the other side of the stadium at gate  d stewards and security were overwhelmed  they tried to use bins to stop fans  breaking through  we counted at least 40 people getting in  other parts of the concourse people  scaled fences to get into the stadium  it's not clear if they had tickets but  fans who were there have told sky news  there were people trying to get in  without  whether it was industrial-scale ticket  fraud as france suggests is unknown what  the videos do show is that the stadium  staff were ill-prepared and  under-resourced to manage and process  the large numbers trying to attend the  game
 

